{"type":"theorem","type_name":"Theorem","number":"5.6.2","title":"Archimedean and Cauchy-Complete Implies Complete","title_html":"Archimedean and Cauchy-Complete Implies Complete","html":"<p>Let <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"F\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D439 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> be an ordered field that\nis Archimedean (<span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"def-archimedean-ordered-field\">@def-archimedean-ordered-field</span>)\nand Cauchy-complete (<span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"def-complete-ordered-field\">@def-complete-ordered-field</span>).\nThen <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"F\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D439 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> is complete.</p>","file":"ch05-reals-from-cauchy/06-the-least-upper-bound-property.html"}